Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL HOS] cgroup: permit v1 migration with target-userns CAP_SYS_NICE

Port the Android common android15-6.6 cgroup-v1 permission exception.
System_server already holds CAP_SYS_NICE but mainline only considers the
open-time euid, so cross-UID app scheduling fails after a successful open.

Preserve the root, target uid and target saved-uid checks. The additional
check uses the caller's capability in the target task's user namespace,
exactly as Android common does; no DAC or SELinux permission is bypassed.
This is opt-in and is not added to the production kernel patch list.

Source: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android15-6.6/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c

--- a/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup/cgroup-v1.c
@@ -523,7 +523,8 @@
 	tcred = get_task_cred(task);
 	if (!uid_eq(cred->euid, GLOBAL_ROOT_UID) &&
 	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->uid) &&
-	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid))
+	    !uid_eq(cred->euid, tcred->suid) &&
+	    !ns_capable(tcred->user_ns, CAP_SYS_NICE))
 		ret = -EACCES;
 	put_cred(tcred);
 	if (ret)
